    "lawCode": "Amd §15-0314, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S354\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to water saving performance standards\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo raise the standards for water-efficient plumbing and appliances in\nNew York State in alignment with federal guidelines issued by the Envi-\nronmental Protection Agency.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Chapter 161 of 2002 to provide that water efficiency\nstandards for plumbing fixtures be raised to align with guidelines\ndeveloped under the federal WaterSense program specifications determined\nfor tank-type toilets in 2014, lavatory faucets in 2007, and flushing\nurinals in 2009. All plumbing fixtures are required to be labeled\naccordingly. Exceptions are made for plumbing fixtures installed in\nprisons and mental health care facilities.\n\nSection 2 provides that this act shall take effect on January 1st, 2019.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\n§ 15-0314 of the Environmental Conservation Law sets the maximum flow\nrates for plumbing fixtures to be sold or installed in New York State.\nThese standards were last updated in 2002 and do not conform to federal\nguidelines.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York is lucky to have some of the most plentiful fresh water in the\ncountry-a fact that is critical to the tourism and agriculture indus-\ntries in Upstate New York. However, we have seen that severe droughts\nhave become more common is other parts of the country and the world.\nOver the next several years, maintaining a plentiful supply of fresh\nwater will be essential to maintaining our economic edge and our way of\nlife.\nIn 2006, the federal Environmental Protection Agency released voluntary\nguidelines for water-efficient fixtures under a program called \"Water-\nSense\" which go well beyond our current standards. At least four other\nstates, including California and Texas, have made these standards manda-\ntory.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.4591-B- 2017/2018\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nJanuary 1, 2021.\n",
